# What a shell `grep`/`rg` in this repo should never walk into.
#
# Measured 2026-11-26: an ontology build ran 130 shell commands, 11 of them `grep -rn … .` over the
# whole repository. The tree holds 1.1 GB of virtualenv, 518 MB of agent workspaces, 423 MB of
# node_modules and 76 `__pycache__` directories — so those greps read megabytes to answer a
# question about ~40 source files, and the hit lists were full of noise the model then had to
# filter by hand (`| grep -v .venv`).
#
# ripgrep honours this file; `rg` and modern `grep -r` both get faster and quieter.

# python / js build artefacts
backend/.venv/
node_modules/
dist/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
backend/pytest_cache/

# runtime workspaces and generated output: agent transcripts, uploaded files, per-user data
backend/outputs/
backend/generated/
backend/logs/

# ontology runtime state: staging trees, backups, retired keys (huge, and never the answer)
**/.staging/
**/.backup/
**/.bak/
backend/features/ontology/profiles/.archive/

# data / dumps / artefacts
backend/data/
*.sqlite
*.db
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.log
